# iOS WebView Shell Source of Truth

Use these paths as the only active iOS shell sources:

- Consumer PWA (`https://beamio.app/app/`): `src/CashTrees_iOS/CashTrees_iOS`
  - Xcode project: `src/CashTrees_iOS/CashTrees_iOS/CashTrees_iOS.xcodeproj`
  - WebView bridge: `CashTreesIOS`
  - Push/badge bridge: `CashTreesPushRegistration.swift` and
    `CashTreesNativeAppStateBridge.swift`
- POS PWA (`https://pos.conet.network/` or `/pos/`):
  `src/iOS/softPOS`

The obsolete `src/iOS/SilentPass-iOS-main` tree is removed and must not be
recreated or used as an iOS Consumer shell source. It was a legacy VPN/network
client, not the `beamio.app/app/` WebView shell.

Do not edit the abandoned native POS business UI in
`src/CashTrees_iOS/iOS_NDEF` or `src/android-NDEF`; active POS business code is
`src/posPwa`, with `src/iOS/softPOS` and `src/android/softPOS` acting as WebView
shells.

Repository/version checks:

- The active iOS shell source is tracked in the `petersunquest/android-init-NDEF`
  GitHub repository used by this workspace.
- The Consumer PWA source and OTA are tracked separately in
  `CoNET-project/SilentPassUI` (`cashtree`).
- Before changing an iOS shell version, inspect the target's
  `MARKETING_VERSION`, `CURRENT_PROJECT_VERSION`, bundle identifier, and the
  App Store Connect build number. Do not infer the active shell from a legacy
  folder or blindly overwrite the Marketing Version.
